{# === LinkFieldShapeRule fixture ========================================
Verifies detection of a plain string passed to a `component_*({…})` field
the component's own `<name>.yaml` declares as `type: link` + `shape: link`.

A `shape: link` field arrives as an ACF link object, so the template guards
on `content.x.url`. Twig resolves `.url` on a string to null, the guard is
false, and the element is never rendered — no error, HTTP 200, no linter.

`shape:` is the discriminator, NOT `type:`. The same `type: link` also
covers `shape: url`, which reaches the template already flattened to an
href string — there a string is correct, and `component_button({ url: … })`
depends on it. Keying on `type: link` alone would flag every one of those.

Every section below calls `component_lint_fixture_link_shape`, whose only
file is `definitions/lint-fixture-link-shape/…yaml`, beside this fixture.
That indirection is the point:

	Until 2026-08-08 the sections called `dialog`, `page-header-image` and
	`article-list`. Those exist upstream, so this fixture passed here while
	failing in any consumer that had dropped them. one consumer had deleted the
	first two and removed `article-list`'s `link` field, so all three positive
	sections hit the "no definition -> skip" path and the count fell 3 -> 0.
	The failure read as a rule regression; the rule was fine. And because the
	negative sections also resolve to nothing once the components are gone,
	they pass trivially — the rule kept zero coverage while its test stayed
	loud about only the count. A frozen, `class: exact` fixture must not
	depend on which components a downstream happens to keep.

Skip conditions:
- `shape: url`, and fields with no `shape:` at all — correct, or unknowable
- an empty string — the idiomatic "no link here", same as an absent field
- a variable / call / ternary — shape cannot be known statically
- a hash passed as a pre-built variable, and dynamic keys — nothing to read
- a component with no `<name>.yaml` — nothing to check against

Known coverage gap, deliberate: the rule recurses into `repeater` and
`group` sub-fields, and section 8 pins only that the recursion does not
OVER-fire on a `shape: url` sub-field. A nested `shape: link` field — the
shape of the motivating downstream bug, `fields → modules (repeater) →
fields → more_link` — is still not exercised. The stub definition now makes
that testable without waiting for a real component to grow one; adding it is
a separate change from this one.

Run from repo root:

vendor/bin/twig-cs-fixer lint --config tests/config/twig-wordpress.php tests/Fixtures/Twig/link-field-shape-fixture.twig

Expected: 3 warnings, 0 errors (LinkFieldShape) — sections 1, 2, 3
====================================================================== #}

{# 1) FAIL: `link` is shape: link — the template would guard on
	`content.link.url`, so this string renders no link at all. #}
{{ component_lint_fixture_link_shape({
	title: 'Kontaktujte nás',
	link: 'https://example.com/kontakt',
}) }}

{# 2) FAIL: a concatenation is still a string. It merely looks more
	deliberate than a literal, which is exactly how the original bug
	survived review. #}
{{ component_lint_fixture_link_shape({
	title: 'Reference',
	button: homeUrl ~ 'page/references',
}) }}

{# 3) FAIL: a bare relative path, the third way the same mistake is written. #}
{{ component_lint_fixture_link_shape({
	title: 'Aktuality',
	link: 'page/blog',
}) }}

{# 4) OK: `url` is shape: url — already an href string, printed directly.
	Must never fire. #}
{{ component_lint_fixture_link_shape({
	title: 'Odeslat',
	url: '#',
}) }}

{# 5) OK: the correct object shape. #}
{{ component_lint_fixture_link_shape({
	title: 'Kontaktujte nás',
	link: { url: 'page/kontakt', title: 'Napište nám' },
}) }}

{# 6) OK: empty string — behaves identically to an absent field. #}
{{ component_lint_fixture_link_shape({
	title: 'Bez odkazu',
	link: '',
}) }}

{# 7) OK: a variable — the rule cannot know its shape and must stay quiet
	rather than trade a silent false negative for a loud false positive. #}
{{ component_lint_fixture_link_shape({
	title: 'Dynamický',
	link: content.dialog_link,
}) }}

{# 8) OK: a repeater whose sub-field is shape: url — a string is correct
	there, and this pins that the recursion does not over-fire. #}
{{ component_lint_fixture_link_shape({
	items: [
		{ title: 'První článek', url: 'page/article-full' },
		{ title: 'Druhý článek', url: 'page/article-full' },
	],
}) }}

{# 9) OK: `type: link` with no `shape:` — unknowable, must stay quiet. #}
{{ component_lint_fixture_link_shape({
	untyped_link: 'https://example.com',
}) }}

{# 10) OK: a component with no YAML definition — nothing to check against. #}
{{ component_this_component_does_not_exist({
	link: 'https://example.com',
}) }}
